Construct a function to sort a list in ascending order without using the sort() method.

def bubble_sort(arr):
    n = len(arr)
    for i in range(n):
        for j in range(0, n-i-1):
            if arr[j] > arr[j+1]:
                arr[j], arr[j+1] = arr[j+1], arr[j]
    return arr

This function uses the bubble sort algorithm to iterate through the list and swap adjacent elements if they are in the wrong order until the entire list is sorted in ascending order.

